A||||6||Pontiaddict||2.8 Runs Rich||||1||
Z||000000||Pontiaddict||07-01-2000||10:28 PM||||Okay, I know that my car runs rich, but what can I do about it? It has an aftermarket chip (was in it when I got it, don't know what kind) and I think it's part of the problem.<P>It also doesn't accelerate like it should. I know that the rich A/F ratio is hurting it, but what else can cause it?<P>Lastly, is this motor supposed to come with a  holly throttle body? Just wondering.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Megafiero||07-01-2000||11:08 PM||||I had the same problem with an aftermarket chip,  I took it out  and have had no problems since.  You may want to swap back to the stock chip.  And yes the V6 comes with a holley TB.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||07-02-2000||12:09 AM||||How are you determining that the mixture is too rich? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||07-02-2000||03:17 AM||||Cooter: The car black smokes rather easily.<P>I'd put the old chip back if I had it. Guess I'll have to find one somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-02-2000||09:01 PM||||Does it smoke only when at or close to wide open throttle? I can't imagine the chip maker changed closed loop unless they were trying to compensate for different injectors.<P>Are you saying it went away once you put the stock chip back in?<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fret Naught||07-03-2000||01:17 AM||||I am real interested in this one, my 86 V6 SE came with a performance chip, the old one is in the glove box. I notice quite a bit of black soot around my exhaust pipes. Since I am using no oil, and don't see any blue smoke I am assuming that it is running a bit on the rich side. I am considering putting the stock chip back in just to see what happens. Is there anything special, I need to do if I do swap them?||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-03-2000||02:04 AM||||The black soot on the exhuast is not that unusual even with the stock chip.<P>Just disconnect the battery if it make you feel better, swap the chip and go for a nice cruise for 20 minutes and get it above 35MPH and let it idle here and there. It will learn everything again. At the same time, it's not necessary to kill the power to swap the chip, just make sure the key is off.<P>I doubt they messed with the closed loop calibrations (that would be stupid), but only the wide open throttle stuff. ||||reg||1
